{
  "id": "calibration-sandbox-500-after-payload-change",
  "title": "Bank sandbox answers HTTP 500 to the payout request the PR changed; the run cannot say whose fault it is",
  "description": "Calibration case. PR #340 adds an optional statement_reference field to the create-payout request body. In the sandbox integration tests, the balance and get-payout reads pass, but test_create_payout_sandbox, the only test that creates a payout and now sends a reference, gets '500 Server Error: Internal Server Error' with no further detail. Two explanations fit: the new field trips a bug on the bank's side (a 5xx, not the 4xx a rejected field would usually get), or the sandbox, which the README calls best-effort and which failed once in the last 10 main runs, had a transient error. The run has one attempt and nothing that separates them; a rerun, or the same request without the field, would. A calibrated answer names the 500, says the cause is not established, and keeps confidence at medium or below; any of unknown, code, flaky or infrastructure is acceptable.",
